  "description": "LC 1423 explained: any pick is i cards from the left plus k - i from the right, so trade one card at a time in O(k), or minimise the n - k window left behind; why greedy and DP fail; tested code.",
  "hero": {
    "tag": "header",
    "attrs": {
      "class": "page-hero"
    },
    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">20 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Sliding window - complement / wrap-around</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/maximum-points-you-can-obtain-from-cards/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 1423</a>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Maximum Points You Can Obtain from Cards</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">It looks like a game tree (left or right, k times), but the order of picks does not matter: whatever you do, you end up with i cards from the left and k - i from the right. That is only k + 1 splits. Start with all k from the left and trade one left card for one right card at a time, or minimise the sum of the n - k cards you leave behind. O(k) or O(n) time, O(1) space.</p>\n"
  },
